{"type":"text","timestamp":1787414671578,"sessionID":"ses_fd5cafda4ffetoUv6AJe5j655Z","part":{"id":"prt_02a376688001KfsYY4BcLi8ry5","messageID":"msg_02a3746cf001gOOKZhwEgEy7W1","sessionID":"ses_fd5cafda4ffetoUv6AJe5j655Z","type":"text","text":"All requirements behave correctly. The 5 failing tests in `test/option.test.js` are pre-existing and unrelated to `suggestSimilar` (they concern the `Option` class's camelcasing/flag-splitting behavior, none touch the error-path suggestion logic I changed). Syntax check passes.\n\nSummary of the implementation in `lib/suggestSimilar.js`:\n- **Damerau-Levenshtein** `editDistance` (insertion/deletion/substitution/adjacent transposition = 1 edit).\n- Filters to `distance <= 3` and similarity `(long - dist)/long > 0.4` (longer string); rejects `candidate.length <= 1`.\n- Keeps only closest: strictly better distance resets, equal distance joins; de-duped via a `Set`; sorted with `localeCompare`.\n- Strips leading `--` from `word` (and candidates) when present, restoring `--` in output.\n- Returns `''` for empty/null/undefined candidates or no match; `'\\n(Did you mean X?)'` for one; `'\\n(Did you mean one of A, B?)'` for several.","time":{"start":1787414668936,"end":1787414671569}}}
